# React frontend

Folders:
- `pages/` route-level composition only.
- `features/<name>/` domain UI, React Query hooks, query keys.
- `components/` reusable presentational UI. No fetching.
- `api/` HTTP client and types. No React imports.
- `hooks/` shared hooks (`useX`).

Rules:
- Functional components and hooks only.
- Server state lives in React Query; local UI state in `useState`. No global store unless proven needed.
- All requests use `credentials: 'include'` and send the CSRF header on mutations. Never store tokens in localStorage.
- Short comment on every component and hook: what it renders / what state and side effects it owns.
- Semantic HTML, labels on inputs, keyboard-accessible interactions.
- No premature memoization; optimize only after measuring.
